"""Durable-state verification for the Android OpenBank tasks.

OpenBank keeps its whole working state in one JSON document in the WebView's
``localStorage``: the signed-in session, the recipient directory, the transfer
and transaction ledgers, the biller list and scheduled payments, the paperless
delivery settings, the alert preferences and alert list, the card controls and
the evaluation event log.  A judgement therefore reads that document and
compares the records the instruction asked for against the records the
application actually holds.

Every comparison is exact and typed: money is compared to the cent, strings
case-sensitively, collections by cardinality as well as content.  Preparation
steps the instruction happens to require -- opening a sheet, scrolling a list,
pressing a filter -- produce no durable record, so they are not judged; only the
records the task creates, changes or reads are.
"""

